# Preview images offered on the landing page, in the order they appear there.
#
# One record per line, fields separated by tabs:
#
#   file<TAB>kind<TAB>description[<TAB>label]
#
# kind picks the icon: "disk" for a disk image, "video" for a recording, "hydra" for a Hydra job
# (file is then the job name, release.<target>, linked to its latest successful build).
# label is optional, the short name in the Download menu.
# The base URL is set by PDIMAGES_BASE_URL, and defaults to the one below.
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.

release.wayland	hydra	The Argon desktop for x86_64 with AMD, Intel and NVIDIA GPU drivers, Wi-Fi and the built-in apps. UEFI, including 32-bit UEFI.	Desktop
release.nvidia-580	hydra	The same desktop with NVIDIA's 580 driver, for Maxwell, Pascal and Volta cards.	Desktop, NVIDIA 580
release.minimal	hydra	A small x86_64 image that boots to a shell, the one used for most boot testing.	Minimal
release.arm64-virt-minimal	hydra	A small arm64 image for virtual machines (QEMU virt) that boots to a shell.	arm64 virtual machine
puredarwin-arm64-rpi3-shell.mp4	video	Video from the 20.5 era: PureDarwin booting to a shell on a Raspberry Pi 3.
